<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01GM">Corollary <span data-tag="01GM">3.1.3.15</span>.</a> Let $q: X \rightarrow S$ be a Kan fibration of simplicial sets, and let $g: B \rightarrow S$ be any morphism of simplicial sets. Then the simplicial set $\operatorname{Fun}_{/S}(B,X)$ is a Kan complex. </p>
